", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1ef7a4cff1dd83405c487627b70ecdd9f5d578759a883637ce460314b627ce47","event_uuid":"9e254f7c-6510-467e-af5f-3bcbe78e8eee","position":{"commit_sha":"547ba32093ce2db33d76a35cbc87fb2699bc0583","position":"1785725082723294001-9e254f7c-6510-467e-af5f-3bcbe78e8eee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Applied plan-review advisory f50cbbec79d137040 before claim: removed the nonexistent binding-walk prev_snapshot dependency, named the actual prev-shape-sensitive invariant/differ consumers, and split their verification into independently testable ACs.","timestamp":1785717296387512001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Test-design / oracle matrix before production edits:\n- Persistence seam: one LIVE pass must write .tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json as exactly {jira_key: {}}; a high-cardinality fixture must remain <=64 KiB. Existing cap-0/no-write tests remain the negative control.\n- Differ branch-2: >=900 prev-only full entries prove the raw differ emits unbound_local creates; the same key-set entries must emit zero creates.\n- Differ both-arm / production seam: {} prev entries may exercise raw field_drift, but run_differs must filter every field-bearing outbound snapshot-differ mutation before Jira; a genuinely curr-only key remains the positive inbound-create control.\n- Invariant seam: check_dual_identity_complete must return identical quarantine/repair outputs for realistic full snapshot entries versus {} entries.\n- Corpus artifact: replay >=4 consecutive real prev_snapshot revisions in both full->key-set and key-set->full directions and compare only Jira-reaching non-empty effects; print a machine-readable zero-difference result and snapshot byte sizes.\nOracle order: add tests/script first; demonstrate RED only at the persisted-shape seam; then make the smallest persistence change and rerun focused, related, lint, typecheck, and broader gates.","timestamp":1785718876736812001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation evidence checkpoint:\n- RED: focused oracle produced exactly 2 failures: the live pass still copied full field bodies, and _write_prev_snapshot_key_set did not exist; 19 controls passed.\n- GREEN after the minimal persistence change: 21/21 focused tests passed.\n- Real-history corpus: docs/experiments/keyset_prev_snapshot_corpus.py replayed 4 consecutive origin/tickets pairs (4df4e28428b5 -> 996b33a1fa1b -> dcb3889bceda -> f3c5a5f3a28a -> c57dd681f8f8). Forward extra observable effects=0; reverse extra observable effects=0; reverse unexpected inbound creates=0. Key-set sizes were 16,288-16,317 bytes for 1,196-1,198 keys, below the 64 KiB ceiling.\n- Production change is scoped to deterministic compact key-set persistence inside the existing persist gate; full per-pass snapshots and cap-0/no-write behavior are unchanged.","timestamp":1785719023303494001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Preflight evidence:\n- make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS.\n- focused A4-2 suite: 20/20 PASS after refactoring-litmus cleanup.\n- related reconciler + bridge suite: 2,018/2,018 PASS.\n- full make test reached 79% before the shell command was externally SIGTERM-terminated at its 30-minute ceiling. A fail-fast rerun identified the sole earlier failure after 4,372 passes: tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py::test_success_telemetry_survives_an_empty_usage_dict, the known unrelated order-dependent telemetry logging bug tracked as d32b-3db5-9fd1-41e5. It passes in isolation (1/1). No changed-area failure occurred.\n- final corpus rerun: 4/4 real pairs PASS; forward differences=0, reverse differences=0, unexpected inbound creates=0, max key-set size=16,333 bytes.\n- five-axis review: no required findings; observable-entrypoint test mutation was proven RED and restored GREEN.","timestamp":1785721800775032001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit review opened: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1256 (commit 43cdab566a, Change-Id I39e0b0984e6560138f9e6365e25bd2e434d9685b). Post-rebase gates on current origin/main: lint PASS, typecheck PASS, related reconciler+bridge 2,044 PASS / 1 expected xfail, corpus 4/4 PASS, commit-ticket trailer PASS. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; ticket remains in_progress until merge and completion verification.","timestamp":1785722086838702001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED + VERIFIED: Gerrit 1256 merged as 6cdd4b00d9ee90b2ffe3e4da4780f81de127d7fd after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments. GitHub Actions run 30777979601 passed every job, including pip-audit and all four pytest matrices. The dedicated worktree is aligned to merged origin/main. Completion verifier PASS/certifiable at merged SHA, with all 6 acceptance criteria met and cited.","timestamp":1785723687863740001}],"created_at":1785372507918837001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3032cf16-bc78-46ad-a560-ba16b7f35f89","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4e3e-d36f-53b9-4c1e"},{"link_uuid":"d1d38ff8-6a8f-4f0a-b781-36498c463f6e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fdbc-fa05-c1d4-4e55"}],"description":"Store only the SET of Jira keys seen last pass instead of the full ACLI payload. prev_snapshot is\n**228.1 MB / 4.5 MB per day** — the largest term after A1. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Measured effect\nOver the newest **400 real revisions**: **218 of 399** consecutive pairs have an **identical key\nset** (so they become byte-identical and produce no commit at all), and when it changes the mean\nsymmetric difference is **1.78 keys**. Key-set payload at HEAD is **19,960 bytes** vs a **27.1 MB**\nfull payload.\n\n## Why this is safe — gate G1 was cleared empirically, not by reasoning\nA corpus mutation-diff ran the real differ plus the production\n`drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions` call-site filter over **four real snapshot pairs**\nwith full prev vs key-set prev and found **zero difference in any observable mutation effect**.\nThat filter is the load-bearing production guarantee: `run_differs.py` applies it before dispatch\nand drops both `(outbound, create, unbound_local)` and `(outbound, update, field_drift)` for either\nprev shape. Its removal note remains coupled to a future migration that passes real local state.\nBranch-3 also has defense in depth: `_mutation_to_batch_dict` reads\n`payload[\"changed_fields\"]` for updates, which branch-3 never sets, so `fields` collapses to `{}`\nand `update_issue(key)` short-circuits with zero subprocess and zero network.\n\n**It also removes wasted raw mutations.** With a full prev, keys in prev-but-not-curr make\n`compute_mutations` emit 973-998 `(outbound, create, unbound_local)` mutations when the fetch\nwindow shrinks or the project is re-targeted. The existing call-site filter already prevents\nthose raw emissions from reaching `create_one` at HEAD. A key-set eliminates them at the source,\nreducing differ work and mutation-cap pressure without claiming a new Jira-facing behavior change.\n\nShape constraint: store a **dict** `{jira_key: {}}`, not a `set`. The prev-shape-sensitive\nconsumers exercised here are `check_dual_identity_complete` and the differ's local-only / emit-both\narms, whose `local_state[key] or {}` guards require mapping entries. The binding walk consumes\n`curr_snapshot` and a mutation-derived adopt-skip set, so it is unaffected. On the first pass after\ncutover the new reader tolerates an old full-payload prev; the same pass writes the key-set shape,\nand the committed full-vs-key-set corpus plus invariant tests cover that coexistence.\n\n## Rollback (mandatory artifact)\nThe committed corpus runs both forward (full -> key-set) and backward (key-set -> full, the revert\ndirection) comparisons. Deleting `prev_snapshot.json` is **not** a safe default escape hatch: an\nempty prev makes the differ re-derive inbound creates for curr-only keys unless a `rebar-id:` label\nsuppresses them. If deletion is ever used, it MUST be followed by a cap-0/no-write pass proving\nzero unexpected inbound creates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Corpus mutation-diff (full prev vs key-set prev) over **>=4 real snapshot pairs** shows **zero\n      difference** in any mutation reaching Jira with a non-empty effect. Tier: **repo-level corpus\n      script** committed under the experiments path.\n- [x] The **reverse-direction** diff (key-set -> full) is recorded on this ticket as the rollback\n      artifact, showing the revert path emits no unexpected inbound creates. Tier: **repo-level\n      corpus script**.\n- [x] Branch-2 regression is gone: with a key-set prev and >=900 prev-only keys, **zero**\n      `(outbound, create)` mutations are emitted. Tier: **unit** on `compute_mutations`.\n- [x] `check_dual_identity_complete` behaves identically for full-payload and `{}` prev entries.\n      Tier: **unit**.\n- [x] The differ's local-only and emit-both arms preserve their intended outcomes with `{}` prev\n      entries, including no field-bearing mutation reaching Jira unexpectedly. Tier: **unit**.\n- [x] prev_snapshot at HEAD is <=64 KB after one pass. Verify: byte measurement.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` (prev persist),\n`run_differs.py`, `differ.py`, tests, corpus script\n\nScope: M. Depends on A4-1.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"persist prev_snapshot as a key-set"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"thread and validate the narrowed prev consumer contract"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py","reason":"regress prev-only and empty-entry differ arms against spurious outbound creates"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"paired full/key-set invariant, differ, CLI, and size coverage"},{"path":"docs/experiments/","reason":"committed forward and reverse real-snapshot mutation-diff corpus artifact"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","4e3e-d36f-53b9-4c1e"],["parent","0303-692c-55dc-4a18"],["relates_to","fdbc-fa05-c1d4-4e55"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","parent_status_uuid":"f2aa67ec-4b48-4acd-b8a7-a2dce940f68f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2cc0-da4a-d736-4ba2","ticket_type":"story","title":"A4-2: narrow prev_snapshot.json to a bare key-set {jira_key: {}}","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["11652335-84e5-4841-9c34-ddfa68dfad59","3032cf16-bc78-46ad-a560-ba16b7f35f89","a9065e2a-0cc2-44b8-9c4a-dafb531be5d3","acbef3a6-6266-4f08-ab00-36038726289c","25b5a33f-1ac9-461f-8de6-6459d458f5d4","a1eb09ce-e9c8-4cfe-8c01-500c24be59d6","eaad1b6e-6bb7-499a-9f9d-35